course: dictionary
lesson: 3415
title: Exposed: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. Exposed can mean open to danger, uncovered so it can be seen, found out, or in contact with something. Read the words around it to choose.
explain: «Lying flat on the ground in a thunderstorm makes you more exposed to current through the ground.» The clues are thunderstorm and current. Exposed means open to danger here, not seen or found out.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. Open to danger fits, but found out as a liar would make no sense.
fact: Exposed means not covered or protected, open to wind, weather, sun or danger.
fact: If something is exposed, it is uncovered so it can be seen.
fact: If a secret or a bad person is exposed, people find out the truth.
fact: If you are exposed to germs, a danger or new ideas, you come into contact with them.
fact: «Lying flat on the ground in a thunderstorm» makes you more exposed to current, so the safest places are indoors or in a metal-roofed car.
exercise: «Lying flat on the ground in a thunderstorm makes you more exposed to current through the ground.» What does exposed mean here? | *Open to danger, with nothing to protect you | Found out for telling a lie | Uncovered so it can be seen | Covered in a warm blanket
exercise: The sun can burn exposed skin. What does exposed skin mean? | Skin that has been painted | Skin that is hidden under clothes | *Skin that is not covered or protected
exercise: A cheat is exposed at the end of the story. What has happened to the cheat? | The cheat is hidden in a cupboard | *People have found out the truth about the cheat | The cheat has gone on holiday | The cheat is covered in mud
test: If you are exposed to germs, what does that mean? | You grow germs in a dish | You wash all the germs away | You are hidden from germs | *You come into contact with germs
test: In photography, film is exposed when what happens? | *Light falls on it | Water is poured on it | Darkness covers it | It is put in a drawer
exam: Which meaning fits «an exposed hillside is windy»? | *Open to the wind, with nothing to shelter it | Covered in trees | Hidden from view | Full of secrets
